abstract: "A source-derived local transaction experiment answering a public concurrency and crash-recovery test proposal. An extracted process-local one-use gate is combined with new exact action/material binding and a persistent, OS-locked local ledger. Five fresh-process cycles test concurrent already-verified authorizations, exact retries, worker death before commit, worker death after durable local effect/receipt before caller acknowledgement, and later historical retry. The claim is bounded to cooperative local persistence, not arbitrary external exactly-once execution or native Shadow knowledge admission. AI-assisted engineering is disclosed."
